fix: close shutdown teardown race in Telegram/Pushover sinks

[TgCsTeardown] / [PoCsTeardown]: TelegramNotify/PushoverNotify (and the
FlushGroup calls) test the lock-free g_bRunning flag and only then take
g_cs. *Destroy (called at app exit) used to DeleteCriticalSection right
after Shutdown, so a decoder thread that passed the flag test just before
shutdown cleared it could enter an already-deleted critical section -> UB
/ crash.

*Destroy no longer deletes the section. It is only ever called at process
exit (WM_DESTROY), so the OS reclaims the section on termination; leaving
it intact removes the race window with no leak that outlives the process.
g_csInit stays TRUE so any late call still hits a valid section.

Updated telegram.h and the PDW.cpp call-site comments accordingly, plus a
RELEASE_NOTES entry under 3.6.2.
